Problems to solve:

Tackle meeting overload. Help teams decide whether a meeting is actually needed, who should be there, and what could have been handled asynchronously.

Key issues:

* Not knowing the outcome
* People not knowing why they are there
* No clear owner of the outcome
* Missing context

Flow:

A user is about to create a new meeting in their calendar app. As they do so, the tool we are building appears and asks them a few questions. Input can be via voice (using AI) or text.

The tool should:

* Suggest who should attend based on previous history
* Ask the user to define an outcome
* Generate suggested topics and an agenda
* Check whether all invited attendees are necessary

The UI should be simple.

The name is “Meet is Murder”. We are trying to reduce meetings, so include a playful element in the experience.
